Done. Added `rename` to `src/store.rs:41` and verified it end-to-end.

**What the function does**
- Reads `dir/old_id.note`, parses it with the same `id\n---\ntitle\n---\npinned\n---\nbody` layout as `save`/`load_all`.
- Validates the file has 4 fields and that the id stored inside matches `old_id` (so a mislabeled file is rejected rather than silently rewritten).
- Rebuilds the file with `new_id` and `new_title`, preserving the body (which is what `tags` are derived from at load time) and the pinned flag.
- Writes `dir/new_id.note`, then removes `old_id.note` — but only when it's a genuinely different file, so renaming onto the same id never destroys the note.

**Verified** (temporary tests, now removed):
- `cargo build` and `cargo test` (existing suite) pass.
- After `rename`, `load_all` returns exactly one note with the new id/title, body + `#tags` + pinned preserved, and `old_id.note` no longer exists on disk.
- Renaming onto the same id is a no-op delete; a missing old id returns `NotFound`.

